<title>USA: Isolyser says Q4 will be profitable.</title>
<headline>Isolyser says Q4 will be profitable.</headline>
<dateline>NORCROSS, Ga. 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Isolyser Co Inc said on Thursday that it is positioned for &quot;modest profitability&quot; in the fourth quarter and that it expects to be &quot;comfortably in the black in 1997.&quot;</p>
<p>On Thursday, the company reported third quarter losses, and that $6.7 million in charges had widened to $0.18 per share from $0.03 a year ago.</p>
<p>However, the company said sales rose 59 percent from the year-ago quarter, and that losses from operations before nonrecurring charges and one-time expenses were $500,000, compared to $900,000 a year ago.</p>
